(1080646, 129451, 16648, '<td valign="top">Whoa - not the worst i''ve seen in this challenge, but you''re close...I hope this is your first entry - yo uhave several easy to fix errors:<br/>TOO SMALL. Check the tutorials on this site on how to sizxe a pic for entry - it needs to be about 600-640 pizels on the long side. DPI does not matter, just total pixels. DPI id for printing ONLY.<br/>TOO slow a shutter speed - the cat is blurry because he moved. a faster shutter speed would fix this (or tranquilize the cat - just kidding!)<br/>MORE LIGHT - this is how to increase  the shutter speed - or go for a larger aperture (small number like 2.8). Try using flash, although that can have issues too in other ways.<br/>COMPOSITION: the placement of hte person and cat is fine, the red bit in the front is what? a barrier to me and the action in the pic and a distraction. It adds nothing. The background is part yellow and part dark - why?   I think it is a couch and you tilted the pic or is it a falling blanket taht was your backdrop? It adds some interest, but is also a distraction. Perhaps without the red bit i''d have a better thought on the yellow bit.</td>', 'Whoa - not the worst i''ve seen in this challenge, but you''re close...I hope this is your first entry - yo uhave several easy to fix errors:TOO SMALL. Check the tutorials on this site on how to sizxe a pic for entry - it needs to be about 600-640 pizels on the long side. DPI does not matter, just total pixels. DPI id for printing ONLY.TOO slow a shutter speed - the cat is blurry because he moved. a faster shutter speed would fix this (or tranquilize the cat - just kidding!)MORE LIGHT - this is how to increase  the shutter speed - or go for a larger aperture (small number like 2.8). Try using flash, although that can have issues too in other ways.COMPOSITION: the placement of hte person and cat is fine, the red bit in the front is what? a barrier to me and the action in the pic and a distraction. It adds nothing. The background is part yellow and part dark - why?   I think it is a couch and you tilted the pic or is it a falling blanket taht was your backdrop? It adds some interest, but is also a distraction. Perhaps without the red bit i''d have a better thought on the yellow bit.', '2004-12-28 23:52:06.000000', NULL, 1),
