(1081503, 129709, 30818, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nshapiro:</b></div><hr/><i> Very good action shot and exposure of the bird, but the scene makes it look too much like a snapshot.  On a studio like background (and maybe with the babies eyes open) this could have been a winner! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree 100% with all of this!  This was my very first attempt at an challenge.  I guess I need to find cheap ways of creating a "studio".  I was disappointed about her eyes being closed, but I couldn''t get another shot with the birds wings open, so I just went with this one!<br/> <br/>Thanx for your feedback :)</td>', 'Originally posted by nshapiro: Very good action shot and exposure of the bird, but the scene makes it look too much like a snapshot.  On a studio like background (and maybe with the babies eyes open) this could have been a winner!   I agree 100% with all of this!  This was my very first attempt at an challenge.  I guess I need to find cheap ways of creating a "studio".  I was disappointed about her eyes being closed, but I couldn''t get another shot with the birds wings open, so I just went with this one! Thanx for your feedback :)', '2004-12-29 12:39:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1081506, 129709, 30818, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> Very cute and adorable with both subjects with wings spread.lol 6 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Too funny!  I didn''t even notice that both their wings were opened!  I would''ve titled it differently if I''d noticed it! :)</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: Very cute and adorable with both subjects with wings spread.lol 6   Too funny!  I didn''t even notice that both their wings were opened!  I would''ve titled it differently if I''d noticed it! :)', '2004-12-29 12:40:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1081516, 129706, 30478, '<td valign="top">That''s ok Skiprow, I appreciate the undeserved 10!<br/> <br/>I probably shouldn''t have attempted an indoor shot, seeing as I had difficulty in discerning what exactly was appropriate light, and how it "should" look.  Perhaps if I took the shot outside, the light play would have been easier- but with much snow around here, I''m sure I would have had difficulty adjusting to the light being reflected off the snow.<br/> <br/>Yeah, thanks all for the critiques, I agree with all of you.  I did use a tripod- however the picture seems rather "fuzzy".  I am guessing that my camera wasn''t screwed onto the tripod tight enough, which may have caused movement when pressing the shutter.  I''ve always seemed to have trouble getting any pictures taken on my camera, in focus, not sure if it''s my handling or the problem lies in the camera itself.  Next challenge, I''ll pay close attention to the tripod- and hopefully that problem will be resolved.<br/> <br/>Bear music, I agree, I didn''t like how the finger overlapped the rock- but I had little to go on since this was really the best of all the images my camera produced.  Next time, I''ll go with gut instinct and when I think it doesn''t look right, I won''t quit until it''s exactly how I want it.</td>', 'That''s ok Skiprow, I appreciate the undeserved 10! I probably shouldn''t have attempted an indoor shot, seeing as I had difficulty in discerning what exactly was appropriate light, and how it "should" look.  Perhaps if I took the shot outside, the light play would have been easier- but with much snow around here, I''m sure I would have had difficulty adjusting to the light being reflected off the snow. Yeah, thanks all for the critiques, I agree with all of you.  I did use a tripod- however the picture seems rather "fuzzy".  I am guessing that my camera wasn''t screwed onto the tripod tight enough, which may have caused movement when pressing the shutter.  I''ve always seemed to have trouble getting any pictures taken on my camera, in focus, not sure if it''s my handling or the problem lies in the camera itself.  Next challenge, I''ll pay close attention to the tripod- and hopefully that problem will be resolved. Bear music, I agree, I didn''t like how the finger overlapped the rock- but I had little to go on since this was really the best of all the images my camera produced.  Next time, I''ll go with gut instinct and when I think it doesn''t look right, I won''t quit until it''s exactly how I want it.', '2004-12-29 12:44:43.000000', NULL, 0),
