(1114139, 129510, 10658, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nshapiro:</b></div><hr/><i> Nothing like the love a child has for a pet!  Good capture, good contrasts.  A few small issues with clarity and flash reflectiosn (all along her shirt for example). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, that shirt is one of her favorites because it has some sort of glittery thread accenting each and every black stripe (both sides) :)  I totally agree about the clarity though, I would''ve liked for her eyes to have come out sharper.  <br/> <br/>I really have to thank everyone for the comments on my first challenge, I''m learning so much from everyone here! -Onessa</td>', 'Originally posted by nshapiro: Nothing like the love a child has for a pet!  Good capture, good contrasts.  A few small issues with clarity and flash reflectiosn (all along her shirt for example).   Actually, that shirt is one of her favorites because it has some sort of glittery thread accenting each and every black stripe (both sides) :)  I totally agree about the clarity though, I would''ve liked for her eyes to have come out sharper.   I really have to thank everyone for the comments on my first challenge, I''m learning so much from everyone here! -Onessa', '2005-01-17 10:05:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1115521, 129709, 1827, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpalitang:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nshapiro:</b></div><hr/><i> Very good action shot and exposure of the bird, but the scene makes it look too much like a snapshot.  On a studio like background (and maybe with the babies eyes open) this could have been a winner! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree 100% with all of this!  I guess I need to find cheap ways of creating a "studio". </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>A fairly inexpensive solution that would have worked in this case is a large piece of fabric draped over the couch and onto the floor.  I use black moleskin polyester and it is TERRIFIC for absorbing all of the extra light. After a little bit of burning in PS, you can''t see the fabric at all.  All of the photos on black in my portfolio are on this fabric.  :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by mpalitang: Originally posted by nshapiro: Very good action shot and exposure of the bird, but the scene makes it look too much like a snapshot.  On a studio like background (and maybe with the babies eyes open) this could have been a winner!   I agree 100% with all of this!  I guess I need to find cheap ways of creating a "studio".   A fairly inexpensive solution that would have worked in this case is a large piece of fabric draped over the couch and onto the floor.  I use black moleskin polyester and it is TERRIFIC for absorbing all of the extra light. After a little bit of burning in PS, you can''t see the fabric at all.  All of the photos on black in my portfolio are on this fabric.  :-)', '2005-01-17 20:21:35.000000', NULL, 0),
